{"key": "62a7256a8af057110eb2f26cc94d99057f1b0e710f73643f0f8e2b5b000f24a7", "value": {"response": "```python\ndef anti_shuffle(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Write a function that takes a string and returns an ordered version of it.\n    Ordered version of string, is a string where all words (separated by space)\n    are replaced by a new word where all the characters arranged in\n    ascending order based on ascii value.\n    Note: You should keep the order of words and blank spaces in the sentence.\n\n    For example:\n    anti_shuffle('Hi') returns 'Hi'\n    anti_shuffle('hello') returns 'ehllo'\n    anti_shuffle('Hello World!!!') returns 'Hello !!!Wdlor'\n    \"\"\"\n    words = s.split()\n    ordered_words = []\n    for word in words:\n        # Remove any non-alphabetic characters and convert to lowercase\n        cleaned_word = ''.join(filter(str.isalpha, word)).lower()\n        # Sort the characters in the word in ascending order\n        ordered_word = ''.join(sorted(cleaned_word))\n        # Replace any non-alphabetic characters back into the word\n        ordered_word = ''.join([char if char.isalpha() else char for char in word])\n        ordered_words.append(ordered_word)\n    return ' '.join(ordered_words)\n```", "prompt_eval_count": 1025, "eval_count": 249}}
